| Metric | Target | Measurement |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| Verdict Compression | 50-70% | Measured via `draco verdict --stats` |
| Quality Preservation | 88-93% | Measured via 15+ quality metrics |
| PEGASUS/BART Selection | Model auto-selected per task | Measured via `draco verdict --model-info` |
| Task-Type Conditioning Accuracy | > 85% | Correct task type application |
| Extractive Abstractive Hybrid | 40/60 split (extractive/abstractive) | Measured via `draco verdict --hybrid-stats` |
| Inverse Formatting Effectiveness | 20-30% additional reduction | Measured via `draco verdict --format-stats` |
| Quality Scoring Accuracy | > 90% | Of 15+ metrics within 2% of human judgment |
| Agent-Specific Formatting | 95%+ | Formatting correct for target agent |

## Common Phase 7 Issues & Resolutions

| Issue | Resolution |
|-------|------------|
| Verdict generation very slow | Use `--model-acceleration onnx` for ONNX Runtime inference, reduce batch size |
| Generated verdicts too terse | Increase summary ratio: `--summary-ratio 0.4` (default: 0.3) |
| Too much detail preserved | Increase condensation level: `--condense-level aggressive` |
| Verdicts don't make sense for agent | Use `--task reduce_tokens` for maximum compression, `--agent claude_code` for agent-specific formatting |
| Quality below 88% | Reduce compression: `--summary-ratio 0.4`, enable `--quality-threshold 88` |
| Model inference fails | Check GPU memory, switch to CPU: `--device cpu`, or use `--model bart` as fallback |

## Skill Execution

### Command Line
```bash
# Initialize DraCo with Phase 7 Verdict Formatting
draco init --phase 7

# Generate verdict with PEGASUS for token reduction
draco verdict --pegasus --task reduce_tokens --input ./my_code.py

# Generate verdict with BART for quality preservation
draco verdict --bart --task preserve_quality --input ./my_code.py

# Generate hybrid verdict (extractive + abstractive)
draco verdict --hybrid --extractive-ratio 0.4 --abstractive-ratio 0.6 --input ./my_code.py

# Specify task type and agent
draco verdict --task reduce_tokens --agent claude_code --input ./my_code.py

# Specify compression ratio and quality target
draco verdict --compression-ratio 0.3 --quality-target 90 --input ./my_code.py

# View verdict statistics
draco verdict --stats --input ./my_code.py

# View model information
draco verdict --model-info
```

### Skill File Integration
This skill file is auto-loaded by DraCo at session start and integrates with:
- `.claude/skills/draco-baseline.skill` (Phase 1 - baseline for verdict generation conditioning)
- `.claude/skills/draco-mcp-integration.skill` (Phase 2 - verdict outputs feed into zero-LLM routed outputs)
- `.claude/skills/draco-tree-sitter.skill` (Phase 3 - skeleton outputs formatted as verdicts)
- `.claude/skills/draco-yaml-filters.skill` (Phase 5 - verdict outputs filtered by YAML rules)
- `.claude/skills/draco-noise-cancellation.skill` (Phase 6 - cleaned noise-free input for verdict generation)

### Dependencies
- Requires: `transformers >= 4.36.0`, `torch >= 2.3.0`
- Requires: `google-pegasus-summarizer >= 1.0.0` (PEGASUS specific) or `facebook-bart-summarizer >= 1.0.0` (BART specific)
- Requires: `draco-core >= 1.0`, `draco-nlp >= 1.0`
- Optional: `sentence-transformers >= 2.2.2` (for similarity scoring)
- Compatible with: All 50+ DraCo agent integrations

